{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39837062",
      "title": "Exposing Nested Functions From The Custom Hook",
      "sourceHash": "73077e9659bdc36ec3edae4a8bd62eea21deb3907899130b59f5d0c74fe07a61",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.51,
          "end": 3.27,
          "en": "So we're using the custom hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.27,
          "end": 7.35,
          "en": "to successfully fetch our places here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.35,
          "end": 11.04,
          "en": "But one thing's missing or one thing had to be removed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.04,
          "end": 16.04,
          "en": "and that was the editing capability of this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.92,
          "end": 19.89,
          "en": "Of course, in this component, we have the handle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.89,
          "end": 24.89,
          "en": "select place function and the handle remove place function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 25.585,
          "end": 27.99,
          "en": "And these two functions should be able to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 27.99,
          "end": 32.55,
          "en": "edit the state that is created with help of useFetch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 32.55,
          "end": 35.97,
          "en": "But at the moment, those components don't really work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 35.97,
          "end": 40.97,
          "en": "as intended because I'm trying to update the state in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 41.22,
          "end": 43.906,
          "en": "But of course I can't update the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 43.906,
          "end": 48.835,
          "en": "from in here because the state is now managed in useFetch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 48.835,
          "end": 53.835,
          "en": "at least this userPlaces state, which I wanna update here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 54.39,
          "end": 56.313,
          "en": "So what could be the solution here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 57.66,
          "end": 61.47,
          "en": "Well, the solution is actually pretty straightforward.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 61.47,
          "end": 62.97,
          "en": "In our custom hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 62.97,
          "end": 67.8,
          "en": "we are not limited to just exposing state values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 67.8,
          "end": 72.554,
          "en": "We can of course also expose state updating functions or",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 72.554,
          "end": 77.554,
          "en": "custom functions that wrap those state updating functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 78.33,
          "end": 82.38,
          "en": "So here to keep things simple, we could simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 82.38,
          "end": 87.38,
          "en": "expose setFetchedData, so that here where we return values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 88.95,
          "end": 91.563,
          "en": "we also return a pointer at setFetchedData.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 94.05,
          "end": 97.5,
          "en": "And in App JSX, we can then of course also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 97.5,
          "end": 102.124,
          "en": "extract setFetchedData here and also assign an alias",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 102.124,
          "end": 104.52000000000001,
          "en": "to that function if you want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 104.52000000000001,
          "end": 107.31,
          "en": "For example, setUserPlaces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 107.31,
          "end": 109.773,
          "en": "which is the name I also used before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 111.39,
          "end": 115.17,
          "en": "And with that, we'll be able to edit this state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 115.17,
          "end": 117.543,
          "en": "that's managed by our custom hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 118.41,
          "end": 121.95,
          "en": "If you wanna restrict the editing capabilities,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 121.95,
          "end": 124.8,
          "en": "you could wrap this state updating function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 124.8,
          "end": 129.36,
          "en": "in a custom function that maybe adds some extra validation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 129.36,
          "end": 132.21,
          "en": "before the update is performed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 132.21,
          "end": 134.58,
          "en": "But here we don't need that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 134.58,
          "end": 138.81,
          "en": "But you might wonder what happens if you use this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 138.81,
          "end": 141.75,
          "en": "useFetch hook in other components as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 141.75,
          "end": 144.96,
          "en": "If we use it in another component and we then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 144.96,
          "end": 148.56,
          "en": "update the state from inside this app component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 148.56,
          "end": 151.53,
          "en": "will that affect those other components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 151.53,
          "end": 153.363,
          "en": "might be a valid question.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 154.38,
          "end": 159.32999999999998,
          "en": "And the answer is no, because just as with components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 159.32999999999998,
          "end": 162.54,
          "en": "whenever you use them, whenever you use components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 162.54,
          "end": 166.38,
          "en": "and it's the same for custom hooks, whenever you use them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 166.38,
          "end": 170.19299999999998,
          "en": "a brand new independent copy is created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 171.72,
          "end": 175.11,
          "en": "So when I use useFetch here in the app component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 175.11,
          "end": 179.49,
          "en": "the state that's created and managed in useFetch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 179.49,
          "end": 181.983,
          "en": "will be connected to the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 182.85,
          "end": 186.99,
          "en": "And if I then also use useFetch in another component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 186.99,
          "end": 189.487,
          "en": "that same state will be recreated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 189.487,
          "end": 194.487,
          "en": "as independent state snapshots for that other component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 195.51,
          "end": 199.71,
          "en": "So just as you can use useState in as many components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 199.71,
          "end": 204.09,
          "en": "as you want and you get totally independent state snapshots.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 204.09,
          "end": 205.98,
          "en": "Just as you can do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 205.98,
          "end": 209.25,
          "en": "can you use custom hooks that might be using state?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 209.25,
          "end": 211.65,
          "en": "Every component that uses this hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 211.65,
          "end": 215.1,
          "en": "gets its own independent state snapshots.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 215.1,
          "end": 217.47,
          "en": "So changing the state in one component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 217.47,
          "end": 220.62,
          "en": "will not affect the state of other components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 220.62,
          "end": 222.903,
          "en": "even if they use the same custom hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 224.28,
          "end": 229.28,
          "en": "And with that, we can of course also re add those props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 229.704,
          "end": 234.704,
          "en": "where we trigger handleRemovePlace and handleSelectPlace.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 236.37,
          "end": 241.23,
          "en": "And I got a warning here that setUserPlaces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 241.23,
          "end": 244.29,
          "en": "should now be added as a dependency here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 244.29,
          "end": 246.93,
          "en": "in this useCallback call.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 246.93,
          "end": 250.71,
          "en": "So to this dependencies array of this useCallback call.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 250.71,
          "end": 254.73,
          "en": "Now, we did not have to do that before using a custom hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 254.73,
          "end": 258.375,
          "en": "because those state updating functions normally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 258.375,
          "end": 263.375,
          "en": "don't need to be added to dependency arrays of useCallback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 263.58,
          "end": 267.596,
          "en": "or useEffect because React guarantees for all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 267.596,
          "end": 272.343,
          "en": "those state updating functions that they will never change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 274.35,
          "end": 278.367,
          "en": "But here in this case now the project simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 278.367,
          "end": 283.367,
          "en": "doesn't understand that setUserPlaces in the end refers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 283.716,
          "end": 288.57,
          "en": "to a state updating function because all it sees here is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 288.57,
          "end": 292.353,
          "en": "that it's some property we're pulling out of some object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 293.55,
          "end": 297.15,
          "en": "Therefore, for completeness sake, and to get rid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 297.15,
          "end": 301.41,
          "en": "of that warning, we can simply add setUserPlaces here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 301.41,
          "end": 304.08,
          "en": "It technically won't make a difference though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 304.08,
          "end": 307.38,
          "en": "because it does refer to a state updating function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 307.38,
          "end": 311.16,
          "en": "and those are guaranteed by React to never change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 311.16,
          "end": 313.713,
          "en": "But to get rid of the warning, I'll add it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 315.54,
          "end": 318.78,
          "en": "And with that, we're now using this custom hook here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 318.78,
          "end": 323.313,
          "en": "and we should now also be able to update those places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 324.36,
          "end": 328.38,
          "en": "I can therefore now remove the useEffect import here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 328.38,
          "end": 332.4,
          "en": "from App JSX and save all files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 332.4,
          "end": 335.218,
          "en": "And with that, if we reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 335.218,
          "end": 339.72,
          "en": "and I add a new place, that should work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 339.72,
          "end": 341.76,
          "en": "Also if I reload, it's still there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 341.76,
          "end": 344.79,
          "en": "and we got no error here in the console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 344.79,
          "end": 348.42,
          "en": "And if I delete a place like this one here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 348.42,
          "end": 350.90999999999997,
          "en": "that also works and it was deleted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 350.90999999999997,
          "end": 354.453,
          "en": "without any errors and it stays deleted if I reload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 355.40999999999997,
          "end": 358.8,
          "en": "So that all works and that all works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 358.8,
          "end": 361.323,
          "en": "now powered by our custom hook.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}